Subject: [PATCH 2/6] fix(annotations): mark the irreversible tools
 destructiveHint: true
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

MCP hosts read `destructiveHint` off the tool listing to decide whether to
interrupt the human before a call runs. Six tools performed irreversible,
outward-facing acts while advertising `destructiveHint: false`, which switches
that prompt off — leaving the in-code confirm gates standing alone with
nothing behind them.

  line_send_message           a sent LINE message cannot be unsent
  line_set_webhook_endpoint   re-routes the live bot's inbound traffic
  line_set_default_rich_menu  changes/clears the menu every follower sees
  line_manage_liff_app        mode "delete" removes a LIFF app permanently
  line_manage_rich_menu_alias mode "delete" breaks richmenuswitch actions
  line_manage_coupon          mode "discontinue" is irreversible by its own docs

The last two are the same defect class as the four originally reported and
are corrected here as well. The delete-* tools were already correct.

Tests: a new guardrail suite reads the annotations back through a real MCP
client — the shape a host actually receives — pinning destructiveHint true on
every irreversible tool, false on the read-only ones, and asserting no tool
leaves the flag undefined.
